ns are holding assets that are  guaranteed to lose value it is a  guarantee that you will lose money if  you hold on to this asset  and so if you zoom out and say well  maybe it's not just the individual  assets that they hold maybe those  pension funds are actually doing okay  most pension funds have an actuarial  rate of return what is their target  their goal of seven to seven and a half  percent but as we know many of the  pension funds in america haven't been  achieving their goals they're under  performing and so if they've been  posting five five and a half six six and  a half percent annualized returns  they have lost money  the money that you have in your pension  plan  is literally losing value it's going  negative  rather than growing as they promised  and so inflation eats away  at everyone's assets  if you do not have investable assets  that are growing at more than seven  percent a year you're losing  on top of that if today in 2021 in  december you do not make seven percent  or more than you are getting paid in  december of 2020  you've lost you are making less money on  a purchasing power basis your employer  is paying you less  and so ultimately what we get is there  are real ramifications to this type of  inflation  there are real problems  people get hurt this isn't a game this  isn't just a number that gets posted  once a month  this is the real life economy  if the official numbers are 6.8 percent  again the off unofficial number is  somewhere between 12 to 15 percent  we can't continue like this i don't know  if it goes up sideways are down from  here but what i know is that if we go  back to what they were telling us last  year and earlier this year this was  never supposed to happen they were never  gonna let this happen it told us not to  worry  so maybe we should stop listening or  start thinking for ourselves we should  start actually being prepared for the  incompetency  and the bad results that show up  when you have monetary and fiscal 